  "summary": "Tracing every interface against the specification, the drawing matches the intended design: the STM32L476RG power pins are tied to VCC/GND with BOOT0 grounded and NRST pulled up by R10 (10k) and shared with the Tag-Connect J1 reset; the NFC sheet shows R1/R2/R3 (10k) pull-ups on SDA/SCL/FD with VOUT tied to VCC and C18 left as '??' (a documented open item, not an anomaly); the display sheet shows the SSD1306 I2C strapping BS0=GND/BS1=VCC/BS2=GND, D0=DISP_SCL, D1+D2=DISP_SDA with R6/R7 (10k) pull-ups, RES# pulled up by R4, and the charge-pump/bias network C7=2.2u, C11=4.7u, C12=C13=1u, R5=390k, VBAT=VCC; and the touch block shows R8=1k in series to A2.BTN with C14=22n sampling cap and SHLD grounded. All passive values, references and net labels agree with the spec, and no shorted, bridged, swapped or mis-valued connection is supported by the drawing, so no anomaly is reported."
}

